      "date": "1912",
      "kind": "site history",
      "description": "An auto showroom designed by the O'Brien Brothers stood on the site, a Cadillac showroom 1913–1921 and then a Buick showroom 1921–1950 — the headquarters of the owner of the racehorse Seabiscuit. Lytle Buick, Berl Berry Ford and Harvey Motors followed. It was demolished in the 1980s.",
